      ],
      "answer": "If validation checks fail during the live patch window for Verdant Bay (scheduled 2026-03-24 02:00-04:00 local time), the system will automatically roll back to the pre-patch ruleset. The rollback procedure involves running the command `orchestrator rollback --target ruleset=<prior_sha>`, which rehydrates the prior rules and replays the cache invalidation hook to restore the previous state. This rollback is part of an atomic deployment process that includes pre-checks and automatic rollback on validation failure.\n\nThe validation checks include running 50 synthetic approval flows and sampling 50 in-flight approvals marked by the customer. Before patching, a snapshot of audit logs (OR-AUDIT-LOGS) is taken for evidence.\n\nAfter rollback execution, the post-rollback steps are to notify Verdant Bay, open an incident for manual remediation, and revert any partial replays that may have occurred.\n\nEscalation contacts during the patch include SE on-call Jin Park and Support lead Olivia Grant.\n\nDetailed step-by-step commands beyond the single CLI command are not provided, nor is specific timing or duration for rollback execution beyond the command and replay of the invalidation hook. There is also no explicit mention of rollback verification steps beyond notification and incident opening.\n\nThis rollback plan ensures that if any validation fails during the live patch window, the system can safely revert to the prior stable ruleset with minimal disruption and documented evidence for compliance and troubleshooting [art_fff67d92fe41, art_f893faeda15a].",
