      "answer": "The financial remedy offered to NordChemica if the 30-day target for actionable alerts per day is not met is a conditional 6% contract credit for the next year. This credit is tied to the success metrics of reducing actionable alerts by 70% within 30 days post-deployment of the tuning bundle and an agreed analytics baseline. The 6% credit is contingent on failing to meet the agreed reduction target and requires a clear baseline measurement before changes are applied. The credit language is to be provided in writing and approved by legal as part of the commercial concession to procurement. This remedy is part of a risk-sharing approach to avoid consolidation to a competitor and is documented in the executive escalation call and the service review plan with NordChemica [art_0a135c689c08, art_ffa7143fb822, art_25fac9f564e7].",
